            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.088,
            0.819,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "**Step 1:** Draw a line l and a transversal t intersecting it at point X."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.417,
            0.114,
            0.581,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.463,
                0.232,
                0.537,
                0.247
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.15"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.256,
            0.792,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": "**Step 2:** Measure $\\angle a$ formed by lines l and t (let us say it is $6 0 ^ { \\circ } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.429,
            0.282,
            0.575,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.467,
                0.368,
                0.54,
                0.382
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.16"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.39,
            0.627,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "How many distinct angles have formed now?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.409,
            0.844,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": "If one angle is $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ , the other angle of the linear pair should be $1 2 0 ^ { \\circ }$ So, we already have two distinct angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.446,
            0.846,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": "So, when we draw another line intersecting the transversal t we wish to form only two angles, $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ and 120°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.483,
            0.494,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "**Step 3:** Mark a point Y on line t."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.427,
            0.508,
            0.572,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.464,
                0.594,
                0.537,
                0.609
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.17"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.617,
            0.848,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "**Step 4:** Draw a line m through point Y that forms a $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ angle to line t. This can be done either by copying $\\angle a$ with a tracing paper or you can use a protractor to measure the angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.68,
            0.597,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.467,
                0.785,
                0.539,
                0.799
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.18"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.808,
            0.846,
            0.844
          ],
          "content": "What do you observe about lines l and m? Do they appear to be parallel to each other?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.844,
            0.645,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "Yes, they do appear to be parallel to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.862,
            0.847,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": "Angles, $\\angle a$ and $\\angle b$ are corresponding angles formed by the transversal t on lines l and m. These corresponding angles are equal to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
